---
import wakeImage from '../../assets/gallery/karman-vortex-street-poster.png';
import ReleaseIdentity from './ReleaseIdentity.astro';
---

<div class="eq-home eq-wide not-content">
  <section class="eq-intro" aria-label="About Eqiora">
    <div class="eq-intro__copy">
      <p class="eq-eyebrow">Open-source computational physics</p>
      <p class="eq-lead">Eqiora helps researchers and engineers turn mathematical models into simulations, with the physics, numerical choices, and results kept explicit.</p>
      <div class="eq-actions">
        <a class="eq-button eq-button--primary" href="/get-started/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="eq-button" href="/gallery/">Explore simulations <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="eq-release">Release <ReleaseIdentity /> · Actively developed. <a href="/capabilities/">See what works today.</a></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="eq-preview">
      <div class="eq-preview__label"><span>Unverified product example</span><span>01 / Fluid mechanics</span></div>
      <img src={wakeImage.src} alt="Cell-average vorticity in a Kármán vortex street behind a circular cylinder." width={wakeImage.width} height={wakeImage.height} fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption><span>Kármán vortex street</span><span>2D · transient Navier–Stokes</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="eq-workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="eq-section-heading"><p class="eq-eyebrow">From equations to results</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Keep the physics in view.</h2></div>
    <ol>
      <li><span class="eq-step" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Define the model</h3><p>Describe quantities, equations, geometry, and boundary conditions. Make the assumptions visible.</p></li>
      <li><span class="eq-step" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Choose the numerics</h3><p>Select a discretization and solver through a realization, separate from the mathematical model.</p></li>
      <li><span class="eq-step" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Inspect the result</h3><p>Follow the run into fields, diagnostics, and plots. Trace the result back to the choices that produced it.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="eq-walkthrough" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-title">
    <p class="eq-eyebrow">One equation, one prediction</p>
    <h2 id="walkthrough-title">Run it. Change it. Understand it.</h2>
    <p>For <code>dx/dt + kx = 0</code> with <code>x(0) = 1</code> and a decay rate of one per second, the model predicts <code>x(1) = exp(-1) ≈ 0.367879</code>. Install Eqiora, run the model, then double the rate and test your next prediction.</p>
    <a class="eq-text-link" href="/get-started/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="eq-walkthrough" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
    <p class="eq-eyebrow">Featured walkthrough</p>
    <h2 id="flow-title">Follow a flow simulation, end to end.</h2>
    <p>Follow the Kármán vortex-street example from exact channel geometry and named boundaries to an evolving vorticity field. Read the source, numerical setup, and result together.</p>
    <a class="eq-text-link" href="/gallery/karman-vortex-street/">Explore the flow example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="eq-paths" aria-labelledby="paths-title">
    <div class="eq-section-heading"><p class="eq-eyebrow">Go further</p><h2 id="paths-title">Find your next step.</h2></div>
    <div class="eq-path-grid">
      <a href="/get-started/"><h3>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>Install with uv, run a small model, and change one parameter.</p></a>
      <a href="/learn/"><h3>Learn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>Work through derivations, physical examples, and exercises.</p></a>
      <a href="/guides/"><h3>Guides <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>Author a model, choose numerics, inspect results, or diagnose a failure.</p></a>
      <a href="/gallery/"><h3>Gallery <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>Follow a complete investigation from physical setup to result.</p></a>
      <a href="/reference/"><h3>Browse the reference <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>Find Python and Rust APIs, command-line tools, and protocols.</p></a>
      <a href="/capabilities/"><h3>Check capabilities <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>See implemented features, tested examples, and current limitations.</p></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style is:global>
  :root:has(.eq-home) h1#_top { max-width: 20ch; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.045em; padding-block: 1.5rem 0.5rem; }
  .eq-home { display: grid; gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  .eq-home p { margin-block: 0; }
  .eq-eyebrow { color: var(--eq-color-brand); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .eq-intro { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .eq-intro__copy { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .eq-lead { max-width: 42ch; font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, 1.4rem); line-height: 1.65; color: var(--eq-color-text-muted); }
  .eq-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .eq-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.25rem; min-height: 3rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--eq-color-border-strong); border-radius: 0.5rem; color: var(--eq-color-text); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 650; }
  .eq-button--primary { background: var(--eq-color-action-bg); border-color: var(--eq-color-action-bg); color: var(--eq-color-action-text); }
  .eq-button:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  .eq-release { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--eq-color-text-muted); }
  .eq-preview { margin: 0; min-width: 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--eq-color-border); border-radius: 0.875rem; background: var(--eq-color-surface); }
  .eq-preview__label, .eq-preview figcaption { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--eq-color-text-muted); }
  .eq-preview img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin-block: 1rem; border-radius: 0.25rem; }
  .eq-section-heading { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .eq-home h2 { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1.2; }
  .eq-workflow ol { display: grid; gap: 2rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .eq-workflow li { border-top: 1px solid var(--eq-color-border-strong); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .eq-step { color: var(--eq-color-brand); font-family: var(--eq-font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .eq-home h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-block: 1rem 0.75rem; }
  .eq-workflow p, .eq-paths p { color: var(--eq-color-text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .eq-walkthrough { border-left: 3px solid var(--eq-color-brand); padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .eq-walkthrough p:not(.eq-eyebrow) { max-width: 65ch; color: var(--eq-color-text-muted); }
  .eq-text-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 2.75rem; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; font-weight: 650; }
  .eq-path-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .eq-path-grid > a { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--eq-color-border); border-radius: 0.75rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--eq-color-text); background: var(--eq-color-surface); }
  .eq-path-grid > a:hover { border-color: var(--eq-color-brand); }
  .eq-path-grid h3 { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 0; }
  .eq-path-grid > a:hover h3 { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  @media (min-width: 50rem) {
    .eq-intro { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); }
    .eq-workflow ol { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .eq-path-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .eq-button--primary { border-color: ButtonText; color: ButtonText; background: ButtonFace; }
  }
</style>
